  "final_answer": "If the backend endpoint `POST /api/noauth/activate` is deleted, this change is **BREAKING** for the Angular frontend. \n\nThe following TypeScript consumers and components will be broken:\n\n### 1. **`AuthService`** (`ui-ngx/src/app/core/auth/auth.service.ts`)\nThe `activate` method in `AuthService` directly makes a POST request to this endpoint to activate a user account with a temporary token and password:\n```typescript\npublic activate(activateToken: string, password: string, sendActivationMail: boolean): Observable<LoginResponse> {\n  return this.http.post<LoginResponse>(`/api/noauth/activate?sendActivationMail=${sendActivationMail}`,\n    {activateToken, password}, defaultHttpOptions()).pipe(\n    tap((loginResponse: LoginResponse) => {\n        this.setUserFromJwtToken(loginResponse.token, loginResponse.refreshToken, true);\n      }\n    ));\n}\n```\n\n### 2. **`CreatePasswordComponent`** (`ui-ngx/src/app/modules/login/pages/login/create-password.component.ts`)\nThe `onCreatePassword` method in this component calls `this.authService.activate(...)` when a new user sets up their initial password using an activation token:\n```typescript\nonCreatePassword() {\n  if (this.createPassword.invalid) {\n    this.createPassword.markAllAsTouched();\n  } else {\n    this.isLoading = true;\n    this.authService.activate(this.activateToken, this.createPassword.get('newPassword').value, true).pipe(\n      finalize(() => {this.isLoading = false;})\n    ).subscribe(() => {});\n  }\n}\n```",
